# Git worktree for new branches (site + theme)

Primary clones stay on `main`. Feature work uses worktrees.

| Repo | Primary (always main) | Feature worktree |
|------|----------------------|------------------|
| Site | `/Users/aronic/Documents/arong.github.io` | `/Users/aronic/Documents/arong.github.io-<branch>` |
| Theme | `/Users/aronic/Documents/hugo-theme-aronica` | `/Users/aronic/Documents/hugo-theme-aronica-<branch>` |

## Required workflow

1. `git fetch origin main` in the primary clone
2. Create worktree from `origin/main`:

```bash
# theme
git -C /Users/aronic/Documents/hugo-theme-aronica worktree add -b <branch> /Users/aronic/Documents/hugo-theme-aronica-<branch> origin/main

# site (same branch name)
git -C /Users/aronic/Documents/arong.github.io worktree add -b <branch> /Users/aronic/Documents/arong.github.io-<branch> origin/main
```

3. Move the agent root into the worktree being edited
4. Linked site+theme features use the **same branch name**
5. Update `themes/hugo-theme-aronica` submodule only inside the **site worktree**
6. Commit/push from each worktree; open PRs against each repo `main`

## Do not

- `git checkout -b` / `git switch -c` inside either primary clone for feature work
- Base a feature branch on `preview` or stale local `main` without fetching
- Leave dirty submodule state in the site primary and then branch from it

## Resume

```bash
git -C /Users/aronic/Documents/arong.github.io worktree list
git -C /Users/aronic/Documents/hugo-theme-aronica worktree list
```

If the branch already has a worktree, move into that directory instead of creating a second one.

